===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|striken||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|striken}}, {{m|enm|ystriken}}, from {{inh|en|ang|stricen}}, {{m|ang|ġestricen}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*strikan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*strikanaz}}, past participle of {{der|en|gem-pro|*strīkaną|t=to strike}}.

Cognate with {{cog|stq|strieken}}, {{cog|nl|gestreken}}, {{cog|nds-de|streken}}, {{cog|de|gestrichen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɹɪkən/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-stricken.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪkən|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[struck|Struck]] by something.
#: {{usex|en|The town was '''stricken''' by a devastating earthquake that left many buildings in ruins.}}
# [[disabled|Disabled]] or [[incapacitated]] by something.
#* {{RQ:Vance Outsider|page=382|column=1|passage=Turning back, then, toward the basement staircase, she began to grope her way through blinding darkness, but had taken only a few uncertain steps when, of a sudden, she stopped short and for a little stood like a '''stricken''' thing, quite motionless save that she quaked to her very marrow in the grasp of a great and enervating fear.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1953|month=April|title=Flood Damage on British Railways|journal=Railway Magazine|page=217|text=Services had to be diverted, damaged lines restored, and materials for coastal defence and relief supplies conveyed to the '''stricken''' areas with all possible speed.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=Guadalcanal Campaign - Santa Cruz (IJN 2 : 2 USN)|date=3 February 2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xY2LC6Rz7JE|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221204001940/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xY2LC6Rz7JE|archivedate=4 December 2022|accessdate=11 December 2022|time=20:43|text=At about twenty past three in the afternoon, ''these'' aircraft duly began to arrive.  The cruiser ''Northampton'' was towing ''Hornet'' at a stately five knots when, out of the sky, came seven torpedo-armed aircraft.  They managed to ''miss'' the barely-moving ''Hornet'' with all but one drop... but one hit was really all that it took, the location causing additional damage to the '''stricken''' carrier and demolishing most of the repairs that had been made to the earlier damage.}}
## {{lb|en|military|nautical|of a [[warship]]}} Having its [[name]] [[removed]] from a country's naval register, e.g. the United States {{w|Naval Vessel Register}}.

